_:genid140 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> <http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#TriggerCondition> .
_:genid140 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#hasTriggerCondition> .
_:genid140 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#Trigger> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <http://www.coresense.eu/doc/CS-115.pdf> .
<http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#Trigger> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://w3id.org/coresense/cso> .
<http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#Trigger> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "trigger"@en .
<http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#Trigger> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "action trigger"@en .
<http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#Trigger> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An action trigger is a condition on the state and/or exhibited behavior of an extended system, identified within a given context, whose satisfaction indicates the need to initiate the execution of one or more actions to contribute to the achievement or maintenance of one or more goals."@en .
# 
# http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#TriggerCondition
<http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#TriggerCondition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#TriggerCondition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid141 .
_:genid141 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> <http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#Context> .
_:genid141 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#hasContext> .
_:genid141 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#TriggerCondition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Editorial definition; the SysML v2 model declares this as an abstract constraint definition to be redefined in usages."@en .
<http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#TriggerCondition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://w3id.org/coresense/cso> .
<http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#TriggerCondition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "trigger condition"@en .
<http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#TriggerCondition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A trigger condition is the condition, evaluated in a given context of an extended system, whose satisfaction fires an action trigger."@en .
